comments.body:
The createReader methods convert generic IOException to FileNotFoundException, which could mask underlying issues. The FileReader(File, Charset) and FileReader(String, Charset) constructors declare IOException in their signature. While UTF-8 is always available and shouldn't cause UnsupportedCharsetException, this pattern could hide other IOExceptions (e.g., permission issues during charset encoding setup). Consider either throwing IOException from these methods like createWriter does, or documenting why this conversion is safe and intentional.
```suggestion
    public static FileReader createReader(File file) throws IOException {
        return new FileReader(file, UTF_8);
    }

    public static FileReader createReader(String file) throws IOException {
        return new FileReader(file, UTF_8);
```
